This isn't a quirk specific to localStorage — it's the same "is this actually a number, or just text that looks like one" question that's come up with form inputs, and it comes up here for the same underlying reason: anything that ultimately has to travel as text (a form field's value, a browser's storage) loses its original type on the way, and getting it back means converting on purpose, not hoping.

