contentSections.body:
The full round trip for saving and reloading structured data:

```js
// saving
const entry = { date: '2026-08-08', pain: 6 };
localStorage.setItem('entry', JSON.stringify(entry));

// loading, later, even after a reload
const saved = localStorage.getItem('entry');
const loadedEntry = JSON.parse(saved);
console.log(loadedEntry.pain); // 6, a real number
```
This is the standard pattern for saving anything more complex than a single plain string: stringify before setItem, parse after getItem. It works the same way for arrays of records — a whole list of symptom entries — as it does for a single object.

