contentSections.synthesis:
```js
const saved = localStorage.getItem('entries');
const entries = saved ? JSON.parse(saved) : [];
```
This single line covers both cases in one place — real saved data gets parsed and used; nothing saved yet falls back cleanly to an empty array — instead of scattering null checks everywhere entries.length or similar is used later in the program.

